<title>INDIA: India produces 41,397 tonnes aluminium in February.</title>
<headline>India produces 41,397 tonnes aluminium in February.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 41,397 tonnes of aluminium in February against a target of 44,278 tonnes, a government statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The country produced 475,731 tonnes of aluminium between April 1996 and February 1997 against 476,635 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>It said the state-run National Aluminium Company Ltd exported 53,491 tonnes of alumina and 9,491 tonnes of aluminium in February, 1997.</p>
<p>	   Installed   February,1997     Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity    --------------    ----------------</p>
<p>	    (annual)	 Actual	 Apr96-Feb97 Apr95-Feb96</p>
<p>BALCO    100,000	  7,011	     83,470	84,570</p>
<p>INDAL    117,000	  3,206	     36,383	56,461</p>
<p>HINDALCO 210,000	 13,498	    149,277     162,230</p>
<p>NALCO    218,000	 15,871	    185,256     173,374</p>
<p>MALCO     25,000	  1,811	     21,345	   nil</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------- Total    670,000	 41,397	    475,731     476,635</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes.</p>
